  "prefLabel": "Res 5302.05 Permission Required to Extend the 180 Day Period for Land Conversions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Res 5302.05 Permission Required to Extend the 180 Day Period for Land Conversions. Permission to extend the 180 day period for changes in land use shall be required from the director. At least 30 days prior to expiration of the 180 day period, a landowner or authorized agent shall apply for permission to extend the 180 day period by completing and submitting Form 5302b, as described in Res 5302.07.\n\nSource. #8441, eff 10-1-05; ss by #10547, eff 3-21-14 (from Res 5302.06)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/res5200-5900.html"
